From e575bec79d510d7ee0b9f915dce2e6c547260548 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:38:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] pin Meson below 1.12

Meson 1.12.0 duplicates LDFLAGS when constructing its compiler sanity
check command. TheRock passes a linker version script through LDFLAGS
for the libpciaccess and libdrm sysdeps builds. Passing that script twice
makes GNU ld process the AMDROCM_SYSDEPS_1.0 version node twice.

A fresh TheRock virtual environment currently installs Meson 1.12.0
because requirements.txt only specifies meson>=1.7.0. The affected
sysdeps then fail during Meson setup with the exact error:

Sanity check compile stderr:
/usr/bin/ld: duplicate version tag `AMDROCM_SYSDEPS_1.0'
collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status

meson.build:21:0: ERROR: Compiler /usr/bin/cc cannot compile programs.

The same libpciaccess configuration succeeds with Meson 1.11.0. Add an
upper bound excluding Meson 1.12 until its duplicated-linker-argument
regression is fixed.

Tools used:
- GPT: 5.6 Sol

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
---
 requirements.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/requirements.txt b/requirements.txt
index bd173fa..89cf521 100644
--- a/requirements.txt
+++ b/requirements.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 CppHeaderParser>=2.7.4
 build>=1.2.2
-meson>=1.7.0
+meson>=1.7.0,<1.12.0
 packaging==25.0
 pre-commit>=4.3.0
 python-magic>=0.4.27; platform_system != "Windows"
